Read the whole answer to "Really quit?".
The answer was read into 16 bytes of the command buffer. A console
simply stopped accepting input there, but from a pipe or file fgets
returned the first 15 characters and left the rest of the line to be
read as the next command, so a long answer ran its tail as an ed
command. Read the answer with the full size of the buffer, like a
command.

---
 editors/ed.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/editors/ed.c
+++ b/editors/ed.c
@@ -924,7 +924,7 @@
 			}
 			if (!dirty)
 				return;
-			len = read_line_input(NULL, "Really quit? ", buf, 16);
+			len = read_line_input(NULL, "Really quit? ", buf, sizeof(buf));
 			/* read error/EOF - no way to continue */
 			if (len < 0)
 				return;
